    <string name="disclosure_title">How Brain Rot uses Accessibility</string>
    <string name="disclosure_body">Brain Rot uses the Android Accessibility Service API to:\n\n• detect when YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels, TikTok or Snapchat Spotlight is on screen, and count each swipe to a new video;\n• notice which app you open, so your limits apply right away;\n• go Home or Back only when you tap a button on the block screen.\n\nIt reads only the IDs and sizes of on-screen elements, never text, messages or what you type. Nothing is stored except counts, and nothing leaves your phone (the app has no internet permission).\n\nYou can turn it off at any time in Settings → Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_restricted">If Android says this setting is restricted (app installed outside the Play Store): open App info → ⋮ menu → Allow restricted settings, then try again.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_open_app_info">Open App info</string>
